{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "#1 - Prerequisites",
  "nextTour": "#2 - Set up a brand in the Okta Admin Console",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Okta org",
      "description": "## Prerequisites: Okta org\n\nThis lab assumes you already have set up an Okta org. If you haven't already, [register](https://developer.okta.com/signup/) Okta Integrator Free Plan under Okta Platform.\n\n\nDuring this process you must:\n\n1. Verify your email.\n2. Set your password.\n3. [Enroll in Okta Verify](https://help.okta.com/eu/en-us/content/topics/end-user/ov-overview.htm?cshid=csh-user-ov-overview).\n\nOnce you are done, you will be logged in to your Okta Admin Console as a [Super Admin](https://help.okta.com/en-us/content/topics/security/administrators-super-admin.htm)."
    },
    {
      "title": "Create an Okta group",
      "description": "## Create an Okta group\n\nIf you have completed one of our previous Okta Customer Identity labs, you may have already created a group named **Customers** in your Okta org. Otherwise, create one now. \n\nIf you do not know how to add a group in Okta, follow these directions:\n\n1. From the Admin Console, go to **Directory Groups**.\n\n2. Select **Add Group**.\n\n3. Enter **Customers** for the group in the Name field.\n\n4. Optional. Enter a description for the group in the Description field.\n\n5. Select **Save**."
    },
    {
      "title": "Create an Application Integration for the Rewards app",
      "description": "## Create an Application Integration for the Rewards app\n\n**If you already registered the Customer Rewards application in a previous lab, you will need to update the Sign-in and Sign-out redirect URIs to the new values that print out in steps 6 and 7**. \n\n1. From the Okta Admin Dashboard, go to **Applications** > **Applications**\n\n1. Select **Create App Integration**\n\n2. Select the **OIDC - OpenID Connect** radio button.\n\n3. Select the **Single-Page Application** radio button.\n\n4. Select **Next**\n\n5. Enter **Customer Rewards** as the Application integration name\n\n6. In the **Sign-in redirect URIs** field, enter the value that prints out to the terminal when you select [here](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"echo https://$CODESPACE_NAME-8080.app.github.dev/redirect/rewards.html\"]).\n\n7. In the **Sign-out redirect URIs** field, enter the value that prints out to the terminal when you select [here](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"echo https://$CODESPACE_NAME-8080.app.github.dev\"]).\n\n7. Under **Assignments** select the radio button option for **Limit access to select groups**\n\n8. Type in and select **Customers**\n\n9. Select **Save**",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 16,
          "character": 152
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 16,
          "character": 222
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "GitHub secrets",
      "description": "## Prerequisites: GitHub secrets\n\nThis lab also assumes you have you have two variables set as a GitHub secret:\n- **REWARDS_CLIENT_ID**: your Customer Rewards app's Client ID\n- **BASE_OKTA_URL**: your Okta org's base URL\n\n\n### If you've done this in a previous lab:\n\n1. All you need to do is [edit both secrets](https://docs.github.com/en/codespaces/managing-your-codespaces/managing-your-account-specific-secrets-for-github-codespaces#editing-a-secret) to add **OktaEdu/okta-learning-brand-your-oci-experience** to *Repository access*.\n\n\n### If you haven't created these secrets:\n\n#### Create REWARDS_CLIENT_ID\n\n1. Copy the **Client ID** that was displayed after you saved your Customer Rewards appintegration. \n \n2. In a new browser tab, go to https://github.com\n\n3. On the Github page, select your profile picture at the top right, then select **Settings**\n4. In the *Code, planning, and automation* section of the sidebar, select **Codespaces**.\n5. To the right of *Codespaces secrets*, select **New secret**.\n6. Under *Name*, name your secret **REWARDS_CLIENT_ID**.\n7. Under *Value*, paste the Client ID value you copied in Step 1.\n8. Select the *Repository access* drop-down menu, add **OktaEdu/es-delivery-ci4d-implementing-self-service-registration**.\n9. Select **Add Secret**.\n\n\n#### Create BASE_OKTA_URL\n\n1. In your **Okta Admin Console**, select your username in the top right hand corner and you should see your Okta org's URL. \n2. Hover your mouse over the URL and select **Copy to clipboard**.\n3. In a new tab, go to https://github.com.\n8. On the GitHub page, select your profile picture at the top right, then select **Settings**\n9. In the *Code, planning, and automation* section of the sidebar, select **Codespaces**.\n10. To the right of *Codespaces secrets*, select **New secret**.\n11. Under *Name*, name your secret **BASE_OKTA_URL**.\n12. Under *Value*, enter **https://** and then paste the token value you copied in Step 2. The end result will look like **https://{oktadomain}.okta.com**.\n13. Select the *Repository access* drop-down menu, add **OktaEdu/es-delivery-ci4d-implementing-self-service-registration**.\n14. Select **Add Secret**.\n15. When prompted in Codespaces, select the **Reload to apply** button. This must be done for your environment to have access to this secret."
    }
  ],
  "isPrimary": true
}